                                "sense_id": "2f55dd74-afd9-313b-bb84-8efd28250008",
                                "text": "The handheld carved figurine is seen holding a patera, a type of bowl, and a cornucopia, also known as a ‘horn of plenty’ – both seen as ancient symbols of fertility, nourishment and fortune – and it is described as being in ‘amazing’ condition."
                            }
                        ]
